TASK CHORE58
	TITLE "investigate running awawa in CI, then deliver in the same pull request the change the"
		+ "user picks from the findings"
	STATUS todo
	SPEC "the pull request body reports whether awawa can be installed in a GitHub Actions runner,"
		+ "from which source and at which cost per run"
	SPEC "the pull request body reports, for each place named in the rationale, the lines awawa in"
		+ "CI would remove or the check it would add, and whether that gain is worth the"
		+ "installation"
	SPEC "the change the user picks after reading that report is delivered in the same pull"
		+ "request, and the report leaves the body once the change is in"
	RATIONALE "awawa is today a local x86-64 binary, 2.7.0 in ~/.local/bin, 1.6 MB and dynamically"
		+ "linked, installed from a local archive awawa-2.7.0+gd66a2ad-dirty-linux-x86_64.zip under"
		+ "the MIT licence, whose install.sh copies its bin/ and whose README gives no download"
		+ "URL; the repository names no source to install it from. Three places would change: the"
		+ "corpus parser of scripts/check-corpus-anchors.ts and its spec, which awawa show or"
		+ "status --json would replace, and the whole guard if lint L016 consulted git instead of"
		+ "the disk; a CI run of awawa fmt --check and awawa lint --strict, which no job runs"
